    <!-- A Super 32X game whose music and effects are made by a Z80 program in the cartridge (0x17B900 in the file; the game's 68000 copies it to the Z80's RAM).
         The driver reads the cartridge through the 32X windows (cart_window; the game leaves the second megabyte selected). Its requests go into a queue of eight bytes
         at the Z80's RAM address 0x1800 (0x80 is a free place); the driver does a step only when the byte at 0x16FF, which the game's 68000 adds one to in its
         vertical-blank handler (twice a frame: at the vertical blank and 0.575 of a frame later, frame_counter_extra), is not zero (frame_counter). The game's 68000 also tells the slave SH-2 every request that it gives the Z80 (the request word,
         sh2_request_word) and, in each vertical-blank handler, whether the Z80 took a request (0x0203, then 0x0200; the flag byte at sh2_request_flag), and the slave plays
         PWM sounds for the requests through the PWM unit; the Machine does the same. The master SH-2 draws the 3D scene and is stopped here (sh2_halt_master). -->
